{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122797","id":4354843344,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA5Gi0A","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122797.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122797/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122797/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122797/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/386e8dc6668a5b1eb811ebde2724a125ddb01e5d","number":122797,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add relevant comments for ifdefs","user":{"login":"voylin","id":56970759,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTcwNzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56970759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin","html_url":"https://github.com/voylin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voylin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\nWhilst going through the source code I kept getting annoyed by the `#ifdef` stuff as some `#endif` have the comment of what they were closing/ending, and others didn't. In most situations this wasn't a big issue as 2 lines above it, the ifdef was defined. But for bigger code blocks it did become kinda annoying.\r\n\r\nSo this PR just adds the relevant comments to the `#else` and `#endif` lines, with in certain cases we add an enter to avoid the clang format stuff from trying to re-indent comments which come directly after an `#endif` line. I did ignore the `thirdparty` folder as I imagine it's not really needed there? Not certain, haven't gone through those files at any point and I guessed that they are \"maintained\" by those third parties anyway.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nI don't know if this code readability is needed for everybody, but I feel like this should be part of the code formatting standard as it does help with making the code more readable.\r\n\r\nI made a python script to go through all files to add these comments, if this would help I can update this PR to add it in the correct place (not certain where that would be though).\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Python Script</summary>\r\nIt's something I quickly put together, \r\n\r\n```\r\nimport os\r\nimport re\r\n\r\nEXTENSIONS = {\".h\", \".hpp\", \".c\", \".cc\", \".cpp\", \".inc\", \".m\", \".mm\", \".glsl\"}\r\nSKIP_DIRS = {\"thirdparty\"}\r\nDIRECTIVE = re.compile(r\"^\\s*#\\s*(ifdef|ifndef|if|elif|else|endif)\\b(.*)$\")\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\ndef process(path):\r\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as file:\r\n        lines = file.readlines()\r\n\r\n    stack = []\r\n    changed = False\r\n\r\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\r\n        match = DIRECTIVE.match(line)\r\n        if not match: continue\r\n\r\n        directive, rest = match.groups()\r\n        condition = re.sub(r\"/\\*.*?\\*/|//.*\", \"\", rest).strip()\r\n\r\n        if directive in (\"ifdef\", \"ifndef\", \"if\"):\r\n            stack.append(condition)\r\n        elif directive == \"elif\":\r\n            if stack:\r\n                stack[-1] = condition\r\n        elif directive == \"else\":\r\n            if stack and \"//\" not in rest and \"/*\" not in rest:\r\n                lines[i] = line.rstrip(\"\\r\\n\") + f\" // {stack[-1]}\\n\"\r\n\r\n                if i + 1 < len(lines) and lines[i + 1].lstrip().startswith(\"//\"):\r\n                    lines[i + 1] = \"\\n\" + lines[i + 1]\r\n                changed = True\r\n        elif directive == \"endif\":\r\n            condition = stack.pop() if stack else None\r\n\r\n            if condition and \"//\" not in rest and \"/*\" not in rest:\r\n                lines[i] = line.rstrip(\"\\r\\n\") + f\" // {condition}\\n\"\r\n\r\n                if i + 1 < len(lines) and lines[i + 1].lstrip().startswith(\"//\"):\r\n                    lines[i + 1] = \"\\n\" + lines[i + 1]\r\n                changed = True\r\n\r\n    if not changed: return\r\n    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as file:\r\n        file.writelines(lines)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(\".\"):\r\n        dirs[:] = [dir for dir in dirs if dir.lower() not in SKIP_DIRS]\r\n\r\n        for name in files:\r\n            if os.path.splitext(name)[1].lower() not in EXTENSIONS: continue\r\n\r\n            path = os.path.join(root, name)\r\n            try: process(path)\r\n            except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e: print(\"Skipping:\", path, e)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nEdit: Just quickly wanted to add, part of my frustration and why I think this can be helpful for are when there are nested ifdef's. Anyway, don't want it? Feel free to close it. Want it but changes need to be made? Let me know.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2304948121,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzA0OTQ4MTIx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:codestyle","name":"topic:codestyle","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-25T05:34:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T07:22:12Z","closed_at":"2026-08-27T06:47:42Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"c9d470664fb06963e0dfb1666879ee6162502d50","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"b